# Codebase explorer: checked spec

The checkable half of [EXPLORER.md](EXPLORER.md), which documents every file of a generated site. The
app reads only these files, so the requirements are about them: which names appear, which pages
exist, and that the links between pages agree. Written in the order of the process (D92);
`deus mdl docs/spec/EXPLORER.mdl` checks it against the evidence in [Laws](#laws).

## Extensions

| Term  | URI                     |
| ----- | ----------------------- |
| `req` | `org.dxos.deus.req@1.0` |
| `api` | `org.dxos.deus.api@1.0` |
| `law` | `org.dxos.deus.law@1.0` |

## APIs

```mdl
api A-1: generating a site
  signatures:
  - Explorer.generate : Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Int
  - Explorer.console : Text -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Int
  - Explorer.pageOf : Text -> Text
  - Explorer.visible : (Text, Entry) -> Bool
  - Explorer.snapshotFiles : Text -> {IO} List Text
```

```mdl
api A-2: writing from the explorer (D82)
  signatures:
  - Comments.isSubject : Text -> Bool
  - Comments.add : Text -> List (Text, task:Comment) -> Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Text
  - Comments.current : Text -> {IO, Throw Text} Map Text (List task:Comment)
  - Assets.isHash : Text -> Bool
  - Inbox.applyOne : Text -> Sexp -> {IO, Throw Text} Text
  - Inbox.apply : Text -> {replicate:Remote, IO, Throw Text} List Text
```

## Files

```mdl
req R-1: names.json lists every visible name once, sorted by name; constructors and operations are hidden
  by: Explorer.Spec.namesAreTheVisibleNames
```

```mdl
req R-2: every visible definition has a page, and meta.json counts them
  by: Explorer.Spec.everyDefinitionHasAPage
```

```mdl
law L-1: a builtin's page replaces its # with _, and any other hash is its own page
  theorem: Explorer.Spec.builtinPagesHaveNoHash
```

```mdl
law L-2: a hash's page is its own page
  theorem: Explorer.Spec.otherPagesAreTheHash
```

```mdl
req R-3: names that share a hash share a page, carrying the alphabetically last name and the others as aliases
  by: Explorer.Spec.aliasesShareAPage
```

```mdl
req R-4: a definition is listed among the users of everything it depends on
  by: Explorer.Spec.usersInvertDependencies
```

```mdl
req R-5: source HTML escapes &, < and > outside the markup it adds
  by: Explorer.Spec.htmlIsEscaped
```

```mdl
req R-6: generating twice writes the same files
  by: Explorer.Spec.generationIsStable
```

```mdl
req R-7: a test or theorem shows its cached verdict, and pass or fail in names.json
  by: Explorer.Spec.verdictsAreShown
```

## Writing and the console

The hosted explorer files comments and tasks as inbox requests, and `deus inbox` applies them (D82,
D93). The Worker's side, sign-in and the request format it writes, is checked by
`src/explorer-worker.test.ts`, which also applies what it filed with `deus inbox`; the requirements
here are the codebase's side. The console (D84) is a snapshot of the codebase directory.

```mdl
req R-8: comments on a definition are kept in the codebase and the site lists them by subject in comments.json
  by: Explorer.Spec.commentsAreListed
```

```mdl
law L-3: a subject is def: or change: followed by something
  theorem: Explorer.Spec.subjectsNameSomething
```

```mdl
law L-4: an asset name is 64 lowercase hex digits
  theorem: Explorer.Spec.assetNamesAreLong
```

```mdl
req R-9: the inbox opens a member's task with its labels and its link
  by: Explorer.Spec.inboxOpensTasks
```

```mdl
req R-12: the inbox refuses a request not signed by a GitHub user, and changes nothing
  by: Explorer.Spec.inboxRefusesStrangers
```

```mdl
req R-10: a console snapshot holds the codebase but not its local state, binary assets or remote bookkeeping
  by: Explorer.Spec.snapshotSkipsLocalState
```

```mdl
req R-11: meta.json says whether the site has a console
  by: Explorer.Spec.metaNamesTheConsole
```

## Laws

Each law builds a codebase in the deterministic simulation and generates its site there, with
placeholder app files standing in for `$DEUS_HOME/platform/explorer/`.

```deus
namespace Explorer.Spec

/-- Answers `$DEUS_HOME` with a simulated directory; the rest of `IO` passes through. -/
def withHome (body : Unit -> {IO, Throw Text} a) : {IO, Throw Text} a :=
  handle body () with
  | IO.getEnv name -> k => k (if name == "DEUS_HOME" then some "home" else IO.getEnv name)

def regenerate (u : Unit) : {IO, Throw Text} Int := withHome (fun _ => Explorer.generate "cb" "site")

/-- A codebase from `source` and its site in `site/`. -/
def site (source : Text) : {IO, Throw Text} Int :=
  List.forEach Explorer.appFiles (fun f => IO.writeFile ("home/platform/explorer/" ++ f) ("app " ++ f))
  IO.mkdirp "src"
  IO.writeFile "src/a.deus" (Compile.Spec.prelude ++ source)
  Export.Spec.deus "cb" ["src"] (fun a => Cli.addOrUpdate a false)
  regenerate ()

def file (path : Text) : {IO} Text := Option.getOr (IO.readFile ("site/" ++ path)) ""

/-- The `name` fields of a JSON array of objects, in order. -/
def namesIn (json : Text) : List Text :=
  List.map (fun piece => Text.take (Text.indexOf piece "\"" 0) piece) (List.drop 1 (Text.split json "{\"name\":\""))

def visibleNames (u : Unit) : {IO, Throw Text} List Text := List.map fst (List.filter Explorer.visible (Map.toList (Codebase.current "cb")))

def inSite (body : Unit -> {IO, Throw Text} Bool) : Bool :=
  Codebase.Spec.inStore (fun _ =>
    let _ := site Export.Spec.sample
    body ())

test namesAreTheVisibleNames :=
  inSite (fun _ =>
    let listed := namesIn (file "names.json")
    listed == visibleNames () && listed == List.sort listed && List.contains "Shape" listed &&
      not (List.contains "Shape.circle" listed) && not (List.contains "Ask.ask" listed))

test everyDefinitionHasAPage :=
  inSite (fun _ =>
    let entries := List.filter Explorer.visible (Map.toList (Codebase.current "cb"))
    List.all (fun pair => IO.exists ("site/def/" ++ Explorer.pageOf (Entry.hash (snd pair)) ++ ".json")) entries &&
      IO.exists "site/def/_Bool.json" &&
      Text.contains ("\"definitions\":" ++ Int.toText (List.length entries) ++ ",") (file "meta.json"))

theorem builtinPagesHaveNoHash (t : Text) : Explorer.pageOf ("#" ++ t) = "_" ++ t := by test 100

theorem otherPagesAreTheHash (t : Text) : Text.startsWith "#" t = false -> Explorer.pageOf t = t := by test 100

test aliasesShareAPage :=
  inSite (fun _ =>
    Export.Spec.deus "cb" ["area", "zArea"] (fun a => Cli.mv a true)
    let _ := regenerate ()
    match Map.lookup "area" (Codebase.current "cb") with
    | some e =>
      let page := file ("def/" ++ Explorer.pageOf (Entry.hash e) ++ ".json")
      Text.startsWith "{\"name\":\"zArea\"" page && Text.contains "\"aliases\":[\"area\"]" page
    | none => false)

test usersInvertDependencies :=
  inSite (fun _ =>
    let ns := Codebase.current "cb"
    match (Map.lookup "area" ns, Map.lookup "Shape" ns) with
    | (some area, some shape) =>
      let areaPage := file ("def/" ++ Entry.hash area ++ ".json")
      let shapePage := file ("def/" ++ Entry.hash shape ++ ".json")
      let ref := "{\"name\":\"area\",\"hash\":\"" ++ Entry.hash area ++ "\"}"
      Text.contains ("\"hash\":\"" ++ Entry.hash shape ++ "\"") areaPage && Text.contains ref shapePage
    | _ => false)

test htmlIsEscaped :=
  let html := Highlight.htmlLinked Map.empty "def f (a : Int) : Bool := a < 2 && a > 0 -- \"q\" & r"
  Text.contains "&lt;" html && Text.contains "&gt;" html && Text.contains "&amp;&amp;" html && Text.contains "&amp; r" html &&
    not (Text.contains " < " html) && not (Text.contains " > " html)

test generationIsStable :=
  inSite (fun _ =>
    let snapshot := fun (u : Unit) => List.map (fun f => (f, file ("def/" ++ f))) (IO.listDir "site/def") ++ [("names", file "names.json"), ("meta", file "meta.json")]
    let first := snapshot ()
    let _ := regenerate ()
    first == snapshot ())

test verdictsAreShown :=
  inSite (fun _ =>
    Export.Spec.deus "cb" [] Check.theorems
    let _ := regenerate ()
    match Map.lookup "notNot" (Codebase.current "cb") with
    | some e => Text.contains "\"verdict\":\"(pass \\\"decide\\\" 2)\"" (file ("def/" ++ Entry.hash e ++ ".json")) &&
      Text.contains ("\"name\":\"notNot\",\"kind\":\"theorem\",\"hash\":\"" ++ Entry.hash e ++ "\"") (file "names.json") &&
      Text.contains "\"summary\":\"A theorem.\",\"status\":\"pass\"" (file "names.json")
    | none => false)

test commentsAreListed :=
  inSite (fun _ =>
    let _ := Comments.add "cb" [(Comments.definition "area", Comment.mk "github:o" "why area?" "t" [])] "comment"
    let _ := regenerate ()
    match Map.lookup "def:area" (Comments.current "cb") with
    | some [c] => c.note == "why area?" && Text.contains "\"def:area\":[{\"author\":\"github:o\",\"note\":\"why area?\"" (file "comments.json")
    | _ => false)

theorem subjectsNameSomething (t : Text) : Comments.isSubject (Comments.definition t) = not (Text.isEmpty t) := by test 100

theorem assetNamesAreLong (t : Text) : Assets.isHash t = true -> Text.length t = 64 := by test 100

def request (author : Text) : Sexp :=
  Sexp.read ("(request (kind \"task\") (by \"" ++ author ++ "\") (at \"t\") (title \"Wrap long lines\") (details \"\") (link \"area\") (labels \"explorer,report\") (assets))")

test inboxOpensTasks :=
  inSite (fun _ =>
    let _ := Inbox.applyOne "cb" (request "github:o")
    List.any (fun t => t.title == "Wrap long lines" && t.labels == ["explorer", "report"] && not (List.isEmpty t.links)) (Map.values (Tasks.current "cb")))

test inboxRefusesStrangers :=
  inSite (fun _ =>
    match try (fun _ => Inbox.applyOne "cb" (request "agent")) with
    | Result.ok _ => false
    | Result.err _ => not (List.any (fun t => t.title == "Wrap long lines") (Map.values (Tasks.current "cb"))))

test snapshotSkipsLocalState :=
  inSite (fun _ =>
    List.forEach ["cache/site/x", "artifacts/a", "assets/0", "remotes/origin/url", "exports/k"] (fun f =>
      IO.mkdirp (Text.join "/" (List.reverse (List.drop 1 (List.reverse (Text.split ("cb/" ++ f) "/")))))
      IO.writeFile ("cb/" ++ f) "x")
    let files := Explorer.snapshotFiles "cb"
    List.contains "HEAD" files && List.any (fun f => Text.startsWith "objects/" f) files &&
      not (List.any (fun f => List.any (fun skip => Text.startsWith (skip ++ "/") f) Explorer.consoleSkips) files))

test metaNamesTheConsole :=
  inSite (fun _ =>
    let without := Text.contains "\"console\":false" (file "meta.json")
    IO.mkdirp "site/console"
    IO.writeFile "site/console/info.json" "{}"
    let _ := regenerate ()
    without && Text.contains "\"console\":true" (file "meta.json"))

end Explorer.Spec
```
